{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLphsLsh6kptdGX5qfHw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `Pow.as_real_imag` in `sympy/core/power.py` so it no longer assumes a possibly-zero base gives a real result. The tests in `test_power.py`, `test_expr.py` and `test_complexes.py` pass (183 passed, 5 xfailed). I didn't run the rest of the test suite.\n\nFor an integer negative exponent, a base with no imaginary part, and a base that might be zero, it now returns `(re(self), im(self))` instead of `(self, 0)`. If `re`/`im` call it back with an `ignore` hint, it returns `None` to avoid infinite recursion.\n\nI checked these cases by hand:\n\n- **`Pow(0, -1, evaluate=False)`:** now `(re(1/0), im(1/0))`. I tested the unevaluated form, since `Pow(0, -1)` itself evaluates to `zoo`.\n- **`1/Sum(1, (p, 8, 6))`:** now `(re(1/Sum(...)), im(1/Sum(...)))`, where it used to claim a zero imaginary part.\n- **`1/x` with `x` positive:** still `(1/x, 0)`.\n\nI didn't add a test for the new behaviour, since the rules say not to touch test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":736,"cache_read_input_tokens":22131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":736},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1726fb81-4352-4667-a47d-cd807e3e5c7e","uuid":"aad4fa06-6fd4-430f-9036-cddec93bfe6f","timestamp":"2026-11-24T00:41:16.996Z","request_id":"req_011ChLphsAiHvoRcm75iECcp"}
